WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.560
Phase 3 trials showed positive results for an autoimmune drug, an obesity maintenance regimen,

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:12.080
and a gene therapy for a rare eye disease. Welcome to the very first episode of Longevity Weekly.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:20.180
Today is September 22nd, 2026. The science of aging examines measurable biological processes

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:26.300
that change over time and contribute to disease risk. The hallmarks framework organizes these

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:33.060
processes into categories such as genomic instability, telomere attrition, epigenetic alterations,

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:40.660
loss of proteostasis, disabled macro-auto-phagy, deregulated nutrient sensing, mitochondrial

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:46.860
dysfunction, cellular senescence, stem cell exhaustion, altered intercellular communication,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:53.820
chronic inflammation, and dysbiosis. The show presents education only and never medical advice.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.920
In this case, every finding is labeled by evidence level, so a mouse result is never presented

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.060
as a human result.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.980
Longevity Weekly is part of the Narra Network, an independent ad-free network of shows

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.020
at NarraNetwork.com.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.580
Listeners can find the full archive and related programs at that site.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.240
Amgen reports a phase three win with showgren's drug candidate.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:23.360
Dazo d'Alabep met its primary endpoint in one of two late-stage randomized human trials

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:29.560
for showgren syndrome, an autoimmune disorder. The result comes from a phase three study conducted

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.040
after Amgen acquired the asset through its purchase of horizon therapeutics. The candidate

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.740
targets the tough-to-treat condition via a mechanism acquired in the horizon buyout. The trial

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.720
represents the first of two planned late-stage studies. No regulatory decision on an aging-related

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:53.880
indication has been reported. The source is biofarmadive. Viking shares surge on updated obesity

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:59.620
drug data. Participants in a randomized human trial maintained weight loss after switching from

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:05.400
weekly to less frequent dosing of the company's obesity drug. The maintenance data come from a

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.320
late-stage study and were described by one analyst as strengthening competitive positioning.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.780
Trial participants largely sustained the weight reduction achieved on the initial weekly regimen.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.900
The findings address questions around dosing frequency in ongoing obesity treatment.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.280
No approval for aging-related use has been granted.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.920
The source is bio-pharma-dive.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.780
Beacon-I gene therapy hits Mark in late-stage study.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:37.000
A pivotal randomized trial of the gene therapy Laruzova met its primary endpoint in patients

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.440
with excellent retinitis pigmentosa.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:44.440
The result marks the first time a treatment for this inherited retinal condition achieved

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:50.220
its main goal in a phase three study. The trial evaluated the therapy in a population with the

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:55.820
rare and potentially blinding disorder. Beacon presented the data as meeting the study's primary

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:02.360
objective. Regulatory review status has not been detailed in the report. The source is bio-pharma

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:08.740
dive. Intermittent fasting shows promise in a Huntington's trial. A small pilot randomized

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:13.600
human study found that intermittent fasting produced measurable improvements in patients with

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.580
Huntington's disease. The authors noted the limited sample size and called for larger

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:23.940
trials before drawing firm conclusions. The pilot examined patients with this inherited

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:30.220
neurodegenerative condition currently considered untreatable. Improvements were observed in disease-related

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:36.340
measures during the fasting intervention. No regulatory body has approved intermittent fasting for this

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.940
or any aging indication.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.940
The source is lifespan.io.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.680
Treating insomnia with CBTI may slow biological aging in older adults.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:52.700
An observational analysis linked cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia to slower

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.240
epigenetic aging markers in older adults.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:01.340
The finding rests on biomarker associations rather than direct clinical outcomes and requires

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.200
further randomized confirmation.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:08.660
The study examined older adults receiving CBTI as treatment for insomnia.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.360
Epigenetic clocks served as the measure of biological aging change.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.720
The source is medical news today.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:21.340
Low cardiovascular risk in early mid-life correlates with better late-life health.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:27.160
Longitudinal observational data from several thousand participants showed that lower cardiovascular

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:32.960
vascular risk in the early 40s correlated with reduced frailty and higher odds of reaching

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:33.740
age 90.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:39.160
The spread and survival outcomes between lowest and highest risk groups reached six

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.340
fold in some metrics.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:46.200
The analysis processed data from a long-running study of mid-life cardiovascular profiles.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:52.020
Researchers tracked frailty, quality of life, happiness and well-being measures into old

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:52.340
age.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.460
The analysis does not establish causation.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.480
The source is fight aging.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:03.800
This week's mechanism organizes 12 biological processes that change with age into a single

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.340
framework.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:10.780
The hallmarks of aging are a set of 12 biological processes whose age-associated changes meet

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:11.720
three criteria.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:18.540
They appear with advancing age, their experimental accentuation speeds aging, and their therapeutic

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:23.220
targeting can slow, stop, or reverse aspects of aging in model systems.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:29.860
The original nine hallmarks were proposed in 2013, and later expanded to 12 to include

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:34.140
disabled macro-autofagy, chronic inflammation and dysbiosis.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:39.760
Each hallmark describes a distinct but interconnected layer of cellular and tissue decline.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:45.180
Genomic instability refers to the accumulation of DNA damage and mutations.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:50.480
Telemere attrition shortens chromosome ends and triggers DNA damage responses.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:56.180
Epigenetic alterations change gene expression patterns without altering DNA sequence.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:03.040
Loss of proteostasis impairs protein folding and clearance. Disabled macro-autofagy reduces

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:09.240
the cell's ability to recycle damaged components. D-regulated nutrient sensing disrupts pathways

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:15.440
such as MTOR and AMPK that normally adjust metabolism to nutrient availability.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:15.540
identity.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:21.460
Mitochondrial dysfunction lowers energy production and increases reactive oxygen species.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:27.200
Cellular senescence causes cells to stop dividing and secrete inflammatory signals.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:31.920
Stem cell exhaustion depletes the pool of cells needed for tissue repair.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.540
Altered intercellular communication changes signaling between cells.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:43.280
Chronic inflammation sustains low-grade immune activation, and dysbiosis alters microbial

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.440
communities that influence host metabolism and immunity.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:52.620
Evidence for the framework itself derives from reviews that compile cell, animal, and

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.760
limited human observations rather than from any single randomized trial.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:04.480
The 2013 cell paper enumerated the initial nine hallmarks, and the 2023 update added three

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.820
more while retaining the same three-premise test for inclusion.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:14.380
A 2020 review examined how Metformin interacts with several hallmarks in cell and animal models,

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:20.680
showing improvements in nutrient sensing, autophagy, and intercellular communication, yet

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:26.000
noted that human outcome data remain limited to the ongoing tame trial, whose results are

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:26.980
not yet available.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:33.680
Telomere studies illustrate how one hallmark can intersect with others, amplifying DNA damage

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:39.000
responses and senescence. But these links rest primarily on cell and animal experiments.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:44.760
What is not established is whether intervening on any single hallmark produces consistent,

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:48.460
clinically meaningful extension of healthy lifespan in humans.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:53.900
No hallmark targeted therapy has received regulatory approval for an aging indication.

00:07:54.680 --> 00:08:00.060
Known risks of experimental interventions include off-target effects on cell proliferation or

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:05.420
immune function, though specific safety profiles vary by agent and remain understudy.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:11.800
The 12 hallmarks satisfy three premises of age association, experimental acceleration,

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.700
and potential therapeutic reversal, as stated in a 2023 review.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.640
Evidence level, literature synthesis.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:26.880
Metformin attenuates multiple hallmarks including nutrient sensing, autophagy, and intercellular

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:32.360
communication in cell and animal models, evidence level, cell and animal studies.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:38.480
The original nine hallmarks were defined by the same three premises in a 2013 review,

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:45.940
evidence level, literature synthesis, tame, targeting aging with metformin, metformin phase

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:52.440
three planning stage, next milestone not dated in sources, Viking obesity maintenance trial,

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:57.100
